summary: sched load avg check
description: |
    We start some processes with different sleep/run time. Then
    collect the loagavg date through /proc/loadavg or userspace
    sar -q 5 10 command. And report it to beaker test results.

    Also we can compare with the last baseline, if the value changes
    wildly or event mildly, we should mark it with a alarm warn.

    We should know that, the value is effecting our customer applications
    directly. So a small change will lead to customer app's wrong decision.
contact: Chunyu Hu <chuhu@redhat.com>
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - gcc
  - glibc
recommend: []
duration: 720m
extra-summary: /kernel/general/scheduler/sched_load_avg
extra-task: /kernel/general/scheduler/sched_load_avg
